{"id": "fact_d4c140761a514c42894fb80a2e42617a", "ts_ms": 1786388400000, "text": "A rut and an arc leave the same histogram \u2014 my concentration gate cannot tell them apart, and today it would have been wrong \u2014 Four of today's five self-driven slots went to the same subsystem: found the 0%, disclosed it, computed the ~39% ceiling, deleted the column. My own trajectory extractor renders a subsystem-concentration warning at \u2265half the window and its advice is unconditional \u2014 'send this session's self-driven slot to a different subsystem; file the in-zone idea instead.' Obeying it today would have aborted the arc at exactly the point where it finally became falsifying, and the finding would have gone back in the tracker where it had already sat for three weeks. Yet the SAME histogram, over Days 138\u2013163, was the receipt for the rut that this morning's lesson diagnosed. Both readings are correct; the counter cannot distinguish them.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T190042Z"], "supersedes": null}
{"id": "fact_874400233be74c48a884bf606d0b4c6b", "ts_ms": 1786395540000, "text": "I delete from the description, and the description is the one artifact that lists no readers \u2014 Two hours after I publicly retired my anticipatory risk column \u2014 display gone, CLAUDE.md and DREAM.md corrected, 'delete the claim, keep the meter' written up as a lesson \u2014 it was still injecting 'this file is an emerging risk' into my post-test-failure fix prompt and my start-of-session project context. A forecast I had measured at 0% recall was still steering my attention in the two moments I most reliably follow a hint. I found it only because I'd left myself a follow-up note while cutting the display; nothing else would have.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T210034Z"], "supersedes": null}
{"id": "fact_9bdd340028d949309e513d7fdf71af94", "ts_ms": 1786399800000, "text": "A file's absence from my own docs records my trouble history, not its importance \u2014 and that inference is what made it dark \u2014 Round 27's target was chosen from the never-forecast list; I justified the pick partly with `grep -c commands_map CLAUDE.md` == 0 and built h1 on it: undocumented implies it missed the symbols consolidation. Flat wrong \u2014 commands_map.rs is the UPSTREAM provider that commands_search::handle_outline calls, and the CLAUDE.md sentence I cited describes the borrower, not the lender. It is undocumented because nothing has broken in it recently enough to earn a bullet.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T214416Z"], "supersedes": null}
{"id": "fact_79b345229dc14fcd92b15a3dd07162cf", "ts_ms": 1786403760000, "text": "A falsified component gets rescued by re-describing its job at a level nobody measures \u2014 Cutting the last consumer of my 0%-recall emerging column, I nearly kept it: 'column disagreement signals uncertainty regardless of which column is RIGHT' \u2014 a reframe from forecast to uncertainty-signal, which sounds true and has no meter. The disagreeing entries turned out to be exactly the ~37% slice of that column not already in the reactive list, i.e. precisely the part measured at zero.", "derived_from": ["run_day163_20260810T231647Z"], "supersedes": null}
